#X obj 667 11 seq.matrix;
#X obj 230 78 cnv 1 535 401 empty empty empty 17 7 0 10 -237178 -1 0;
#X text 240 83 A sequencer intended to drive a [ui.matrix] object:
on each tick it advances its position by one step \, sends the column
index to the matrix \, and outputs a bang so that the corresponding
column is highlighted and can trigger sound. The pattern length is
set with the argument N or the @n property \, and the timing is controlled
by @t (interval between steps) and @div (beat subdivision).;
#X text 240 214 Typical use cases:;
#X text 250 239 • Grid-based step sequencer — building a classic step
sequencer where each column of the matrix corresponds to one step \,
and the highlighted column triggers its sound on the current step.;
#X text 250 309 • Multi-track drum patterns — driving several rows
of the matrix as independent percussion voices \, so that one moving
column triggers a kick \, snare \, hi-hat and so on at the right moments.;
#X text 250 379 • Visual feedback for algorithmic patterns — pairing
the sequencer with a pattern generator (for example \, [seq.life] or
[seq.bangs]) \, so that the matrix shows the current state and the
moving cursor highlights the active column.;
